.TH XASM "1" "September 2026" "xasm 1.7.0" "XORcyst Manual"
.SH NAME
xasm \- assembler for 6502 machine code
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xasm
[\fI\,OPTION\/\fR...] \fI\,FILE\/\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
The XORcyst Assembler \fB\-\-\fR it kicks the 6502's ass
.PP
\fB\-D\fR, \fB\-\-define=IDENT\fR[=\fI\,VALUE\/\fR] Define IDENT
\fB\-I\fR, \fB\-\-include\-path\fR=\fI\,DIR\/\fR     Specify a search path for include files
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR=\fI\,FILE\/\fR          Output to FILE instead of standard output
.TP
\fB\-\-listing\fR=\fI\,FILE\/\fR
Generate listing file
.TP
\fB\-\-listing\-format\fR=\fI\,FMT\/\fR
Listing format: text|json|ndjson
.TP
\fB\-\-xref\fR=\fI\,FILE\/\fR
Generate cross\-reference output
.TP
\fB\-\-xref\-format\fR=\fI\,FMT\/\fR
Xref format: text|csv|json
.TP
\fB\-\-xref\-data\fR=\fI\,BOOL\/\fR
Extend JSON xref with data read/write edges
.TP
\fB\-\-xref\-instructions\fR=\fI\,BOOL\/\fR
Include versioned instruction/operand records
.TP
\fB\-\-instruction\-records\-output\fR=\fI\,FILE\/\fR
Separate instruction JSON (requires dependency manifest)
.TP
\fB\-\-fceux\-nl\-rom\-prefix\fR=\fI\,PREFIX\/\fR
Write FCEUX .nl labels for resolved addresses
>= $8000 to PREFIX<bank>.nl, one file per
16KB page of the raw PRG image (hex bank
number, starting at 0)
.TP
\fB\-\-fceux\-nl\-ram\-output\fR=\fI\,FILE\/\fR
FCEUX .nl labels for resolved addresses < $8000
.TP
\fB\-\-fceux\-nl\-mirror\-16k\fR
Name both CPU windows of a 16KB NROM image
($8000\-$BFFF and $C000\-$FFFF;
requires exactly 16384 PRG bytes)
.TP
\fB\-\-dependency\-manifest\fR=\fI\,FILE\/\fR
Snapshot/hash consumed inputs (pure\-binary v1)
.TP
\fB\-\-xref\-include\-locals\fR=\fI\,BOOL\/\fR
Include local labels in xref (default false)
.TP
\fB\-\-xref\-include\-anon\fR=\fI\,BOOL\/\fR
Include anonymous labels in xref (default false)
.TP
\fB\-\-xref\-summary\fR
Generate cross\-reference summary
.TP
\fB\-\-xref\-summary\-output\fR=\fI\,FILE\/\fR
Write summary to FILE (default stdout)
.TP
\fB\-\-xref\-summary\-format\fR=\fI\,FMT\/\fR
Summary format: json|ndjson|text (default json)
.TP
\fB\-\-xref\-summary\-kind\fR=\fI\,KIND\/\fR
Filter: callable|jump_target|data|all (default all)
.HP
\fB\-\-xref\-summary\-limit\fR=\fI\,N\/\fR Entries per section (default 25)
.TP
\fB\-\-xref\-summary\-top\-referrers\fR=\fI\,N\/\fR
Top referrers per entry (default 5)
.TP
\fB\-\-xref\-summary\-nearby\-window\fR=\fI\,BYTES\/\fR
Nearby symbol window (default 128)
.TP
\fB\-\-xref\-summary\-include\fR=\fI\,REGEX\/\fR
Include symbols matching regex
.TP
\fB\-\-xref\-summary\-exclude\fR=\fI\,REGEX\/\fR
Exclude symbols matching regex
.TP
\fB\-\-analyze\-index\-patterns\fR
Analyze indexed direct table accesses
.TP
\fB\-\-index\-patterns\-output\fR=\fI\,FILE\/\fR
Write index\-pattern analysis to FILE (default stdout)
.TP
\fB\-\-index\-patterns\-format\fR=\fI\,FMT\/\fR
Index\-pattern format: json|ndjson|text (default json)
.TP
\fB\-\-index\-patterns\-split\-pairs\fR=\fI\,PAIRS\/\fR
Split\-table suffix pairs, e.g. Lo:Hi,_lo:_hi
.TP
\fB\-\-data\-consumers\fR
Aggregate direct data consumers by symbol span
.TP
\fB\-\-data\-consumers\-output\fR=\fI\,FILE\/\fR
Write data\-consumer analysis to FILE (default stdout)
.TP
\fB\-\-data\-consumers\-format\fR=\fI\,FMT\/\fR
Data\-consumer format: json|ndjson|text (default json)
.TP
\fB\-\-analyze\-data\-coverage\fR
Report span coverage metrics only
.TP
\fB\-\-data\-coverage\-output\fR=\fI\,FILE\/\fR
Write data\-coverage analysis to FILE (default stdout)
.TP
\fB\-\-data\-coverage\-format\fR=\fI\,FMT\/\fR
Data\-coverage format: json|ndjson|text (default json)
.TP
\fB\-\-include\-locals\fR=\fI\,BOOL\/\fR
Include local labels (default false)
.TP
\fB\-\-include\-anon\fR=\fI\,BOOL\/\fR
Include anonymous labels (default false)
.HP
\fB\-\-include\-overlaps\fR=\fI\,BOOL\/\fR Include overlap symbols in span analyses (default false)
.TP
\fB\-\-audit\-raw\-addresses\fR
Enable raw\-address audit diagnostics
.TP
\fB\-\-audit\-level\fR=\fI\,LVL\/\fR
Audit severity level: warn|error
.TP
\fB\-\-audit\-rom\-range\fR=\fI\,RNG\/\fR
Audit ROM range, e.g. $C000\-$FFFF
.TP
\fB\-\-audit\-output\-format\fR=\fI\,FMT\/\fR
Audit output format: text|json
.TP
\fB\-\-compare\fR=\fI\,FILE\/\fR
Compare assembled output with FILE
.TP
\fB\-\-compare\-offset\fR=\fI\,N\/\fR
Compare start offset in bytes (default 0)
.TP
\fB\-\-compare\-length\fR=\fI\,N\/\fR
Compare byte count (default auto)
.TP
\fB\-\-compare\-max\-mismatches\fR=\fI\,N\/\fR
Maximum mismatches reported (default 1)
.TP
\fB\-\-compare\-format\fR=\fI\,FMT\/\fR
Compare output format: text|json
.TP
\fB\-\-compare\-cpu\-base\fR=\fI\,ADDR\/\fR
Fallback CPU base address (e.g. $C000)
.TP
\fB\-\-warn\-unused\-equ\fR
Warn on unused EQU symbols (W0201)
.TP
\fB\-\-Werror\fR=\fI\,unused\-equ\/\fR
Promote unused EQU warnings to errors
.TP
\fB\-\-Wno\-unused\-equ\fR
Disable unused EQU warnings
.TP
\fB\-\-pure\-binary\fR
Output pure 6502 binary
.TP
\fB\-\-swap\-parens\fR
Use ( ) instead of [ ] for indirection
.TP
\fB\-\-case\-insensitive\fR
Case\-insensitive identifiers
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-warn\fR
Suppress warnings
.PP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR, \fB\-\-silent\fR  Don't produce any output
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR              Produce verbose output
\fB\-g\fR, \fB\-\-debug\fR                Retain file locations
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Give this help list
.TP
\fB\-\-usage\fR
Give a short usage message
.PP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR              Print program version
.PP
Mandatory or optional arguments to long options are also mandatory or optional
for any corresponding short options.
